WEBVTT

00:00:00.035 --> 00:00:02.438
An autonomous build lets an agent continue through an

00:00:02.508 --> 00:00:05.190
authorized sequence without asking for routine

00:00:05.236 --> 00:00:06.606
confirmation at every step.

00:00:07.117 --> 00:00:09.218
It does not grant unlimited permission.

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:12.945
Define the goal, the approved scope, the definition of

00:00:13.014 --> 00:00:15.998
done, a deadline if relevant, and what actions are

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:16.486
allowed.

00:00:16.927 --> 00:00:19.214
For the tracker, autonomous work might include

00:00:19.249 --> 00:00:21.281
implementing and testing a local feature.

00:00:21.722 --> 00:00:24.996
It does not automatically authorize sending real messages,

00:00:25.321 --> 00:00:28.642
buying a service, granting credentials, or changing an

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:29.652
unrelated system.

00:00:29.945 --> 00:00:34.891
A useful loop is plan, build, review, fix, verify, and

00:00:34.949 --> 00:00:35.518
record.

00:00:35.959 --> 00:00:38.966
Work in small slices, and persist a checkpoint at

00:00:39.024 --> 00:00:40.115
meaningful milestones.

00:00:40.626 --> 00:00:43.343
A checkpoint is durable information that survives a

00:00:43.424 --> 00:00:47.720
session ending: current revision, completed work, checks,

00:00:47.871 --> 00:00:51.946
active processes, uncertain effects, usage where visible,

00:00:52.329 --> 00:00:54.976
rollback information, and the next safe action.

00:00:55.673 --> 00:00:58.459
A fresh agent should be able to resume from it without

00:00:58.494 --> 00:01:00.061
treating the workspace as empty.

00:01:00.352 --> 00:01:01.838
Some decisions need the owner.

00:01:02.163 --> 00:01:05.228
Write a Morning Unblock item containing the exact blocker,

00:01:05.507 --> 00:01:08.456
what was completed up to the boundary, and one action the

00:01:08.502 --> 00:01:09.315
owner must take.

00:01:09.756 --> 00:01:12.670
Keep that feature inactive if necessary and continue

00:01:12.728 --> 00:01:14.295
independent authorized work.

00:01:14.806 --> 00:01:17.836
If all remaining work requires approval or crosses a

00:01:17.929 --> 00:01:20.867
safety boundary, stop and report the blocker.

00:01:21.563 --> 00:01:24.733
Do not invent credentials or pretend a mock integration is

00:01:24.849 --> 00:01:26.857
live just to keep the loop moving.

00:01:27.127 --> 00:01:29.286
Suppose an agent was interrupted after submitting a

00:01:29.344 --> 00:01:30.412
request to a provider.

00:01:30.796 --> 00:01:32.920
You may not know whether the provider accepted it.

00:01:33.303 --> 00:01:35.637
Blindly resending can duplicate the effect.

00:01:36.078 --> 00:01:39.352
First inspect the job, logs, and durable records;

00:01:39.793 --> 00:01:40.989
reconcile what happened.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:44.170
The same principle applies to a worker that may have

00:01:44.205 --> 00:01:46.283
committed changes before a session ended.

00:01:46.724 --> 00:01:51.275
Preserve valid work, identify the first unproven step, and

00:01:51.333 --> 00:01:54.236
only retry when the operation is safe to repeat.

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:57.676
Check visible shared usage before substantial dispatch and

00:01:57.711 --> 00:01:58.512
after batches.

00:01:58.953 --> 00:02:02.668
Dave's example reserves 25 percent and stops discretionary

00:02:02.715 --> 00:02:06.326
cloud dispatch at 75 percent used; your own policy can

00:02:06.372 --> 00:02:06.790
differ.

00:02:07.115 --> 00:02:09.855
At the threshold, continue safe independent work through

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:12.943
available deterministic or local means and preserve

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:16.984
capacity for essential completion, recovery, and handoff.

00:02:17.587 --> 00:02:21.361
If usage is unknown, avoid discretionary cloud dispatch

00:02:21.419 --> 00:02:24.646
and retain only the minimum authorized cloud work needed

00:02:24.971 --> 00:02:26.887
for safe completion and handoff.

00:02:27.398 --> 00:02:30.463
The exact behavior must respect the actual platform and

00:02:30.498 --> 00:02:31.484
the owner's permissions.

00:02:31.754 --> 00:02:34.563
At the end, report the outcome and links, revision,

00:02:34.889 --> 00:02:38.789
completed and pending work, tests and evidence, actual

00:02:38.882 --> 00:02:43.503
model routes and exposed usage, assumptions, blockers,

00:02:43.886 --> 00:02:47.764
uncertain external effects, rollback, and the next safe

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:48.310
action.

00:02:49.007 --> 00:02:51.561
Label offline and live evidence correctly.

00:02:51.944 --> 00:02:54.487
Include the first few things the owner should inspect.

00:02:54.928 --> 00:02:57.830
If a deadline or blocker ends the run early, say so

00:02:57.888 --> 00:02:58.422
plainly.

00:02:58.806 --> 00:03:02.347
Completion is a proven state, not a confident sentence.

00:03:02.683 --> 00:03:06.177
Start with the approved definition of done: for example,

00:03:06.224 --> 00:03:09.626
implement the fictional tracker locally, cover the agreed

00:03:09.649 --> 00:03:13.016
acceptance cases, and produce a restartable handoff.

00:03:13.712 --> 00:03:17.868
State the authorized workspace, the documents to read, any

00:03:17.938 --> 00:03:20.237
deadline, and a compact work loop.

00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:24.045
Tell the agent to make reasonable reversible decisions

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:25.694
within scope and record them.

00:03:26.297 --> 00:03:29.037
Also state which decisions require the owner.

00:03:29.362 --> 00:03:33.043
A phrase like "do not stop" cannot authorize buying

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:35.585
services or altering unrelated systems.

00:03:35.833 --> 00:03:38.921
After a verified slice, record the revision, changed

00:03:38.956 --> 00:03:43.228
behavior, tests and outcomes, current status, next task,

00:03:43.437 --> 00:03:44.552
and relevant usage.

00:03:45.249 --> 00:03:48.569
If an external operation occurred, record its known or

00:03:48.639 --> 00:03:50.903
uncertain state without exposing secrets.

00:03:51.506 --> 00:03:54.397
A checkpoint can be a progress file or another durable

00:03:54.443 --> 00:03:56.046
record appropriate to the project.

00:03:56.487 --> 00:03:59.679
It should be updated before context is lost, not only at

00:03:59.714 --> 00:04:00.446
the very end.

00:04:00.887 --> 00:04:04.022
Small verified commits can supplement the checkpoint when

00:04:04.045 --> 00:04:06.123
the repository workflow permits them.

00:04:06.433 --> 00:04:09.057
Imagine the private view can be built locally but the

00:04:09.104 --> 00:04:12.413
chosen identity provider requires a credential the owner

00:04:12.471 --> 00:04:13.481
has not granted.

00:04:13.922 --> 00:04:17.509
Record "Owner action: provide or approve the named access"

00:04:17.718 --> 00:04:19.866
and leave the real integration inactive.

00:04:20.307 --> 00:04:23.941
Continue documentation, synthetic tests, and independent

00:04:23.988 --> 00:04:26.344
interface work that does not require the credential.

00:04:26.855 --> 00:04:29.909
When nothing useful remains within scope, stop with the

00:04:29.955 --> 00:04:31.000
precise blocker.

00:04:31.697 --> 00:04:35.098
Never label the real identity integration complete because

00:04:35.122 --> 00:04:36.410
a fake test passed.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:39.107
A timeout does not always mean nothing happened.

00:04:39.548 --> 00:04:43.112
If a real provider request may have succeeded, inspect the

00:04:43.147 --> 00:04:46.166
provider's record or a durable operation log through

00:04:46.224 --> 00:04:48.604
authorized read-only means before retrying.

00:04:49.207 --> 00:04:52.598
If the outcome remains uncertain, report that state and

00:04:52.633 --> 00:04:54.711
the exact action needed to resolve it.

00:04:55.314 --> 00:04:58.229
An idempotency key or similar design can make repeated

00:04:58.287 --> 00:05:01.305
requests safer, but it must actually be supported and

00:05:01.363 --> 00:05:01.781
used.

00:05:02.164 --> 00:05:04.846
Do not claim an operation is safe to repeat based on a

00:05:04.893 --> 00:05:05.496
name alone.

00:05:05.847 --> 00:05:08.285
Before a batch, inspect exposed account usage.

00:05:08.726 --> 00:05:11.861
After the batch, record its outcomes and current usage if

00:05:11.907 --> 00:05:12.442
visible.

00:05:12.883 --> 00:05:16.609
Dave's default reserves 25 percent and stops discretionary

00:05:16.656 --> 00:05:20.603
cloud dispatch at 75 percent used; it is not a universal

00:05:20.661 --> 00:05:21.555
platform rule.

00:05:22.066 --> 00:05:24.190
Do not consume reset credits automatically.

00:05:24.364 --> 00:05:27.650
If usage cannot be checked, keep the state unknown and use

00:05:27.685 --> 00:05:28.695
conservative routes.

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:33.385
A reserve exists so integration, review, safe recovery,

00:05:33.409 --> 00:05:35.568
and handoff are not stranded at the end.

00:05:35.865 --> 00:05:38.152
Write the report for a person who was asleep while the

00:05:38.187 --> 00:05:38.860
work happened.

00:05:39.301 --> 00:05:42.622
Put the outcome and artifact links first, followed by what

00:05:42.668 --> 00:05:45.826
is built, verified, unverified, or blocked.

00:05:46.267 --> 00:05:49.669
Include checks and evidence, the actual route and usage if

00:05:49.727 --> 00:05:54.476
exposed, decisions taken, unresolved effects, rollback,

00:05:54.557 --> 00:05:55.602
and the next action.

00:05:56.206 --> 00:05:58.806
Make the first few things to inspect easy to find.

00:05:59.248 --> 00:06:02.533
If the job ran out of time, report partial completion

00:06:02.649 --> 00:06:05.842
accurately rather than stretching the definition of done.

00:06:06.141 --> 00:06:09.241
In the morning, the owner or a fresh agent should compare

00:06:09.276 --> 00:06:11.296
the handoff with the actual workspace.

00:06:11.737 --> 00:06:15.417
Check the revision, working changes, running jobs, and

00:06:15.487 --> 00:06:17.414
evidence before choosing the next action.

00:06:18.018 --> 00:06:21.269
If the handoff says a test passed but later code changes

00:06:21.338 --> 00:06:24.833
touched that behavior, the earlier result may no longer be

00:06:24.868 --> 00:06:25.437
sufficient.

00:06:25.878 --> 00:06:29.546
If an external operation is uncertain, reconcile it first.

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:33.355
This short reality check preserves valid progress while

00:06:33.389 --> 00:06:35.990
preventing duplicate work or duplicate effects.
